1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:05,854
Running Bolna open source with Docker, but your local setup never places a call?

2
00:00:05,984 --> 00:00:08,784
The documented setup is four containers.

3
00:00:08,914 --> 00:00:13,464
One .env file and one ngrok authtoken wire them together.

4
00:00:13,594 --> 00:00:22,248
This episode walks through the Docker setup, for Twilio or
Plivo, step by step, straight from the repo's local setup docs.

5
00:00:26,498 --> 00:00:32,776
First, a telephony web server. For Twilio, that is twilio app, on port 8001.

6
00:00:32,906 --> 00:00:39,787
For Plivo, it is plivo app, on port 8002.
Either way, you need an account with that provider.

7
00:00:39,917 --> 00:00:46,906
Second, the Bolna server. Bolna app, on port 5001, creates and handles your agents.

8
00:00:47,036 --> 00:00:54,210
Third, Redis, on port 6379. It persists your agents and prompt data.

9
00:00:54,340 --> 00:01:05,253
And fourth, ngrok, for tunneling. Its config defines a tunnel for each of
the three apps. The telephony servers depend on Redis, ngrok, and the Bolna app.

10
00:01:05,903 --> 00:01:07,283
Gather these first.

11
00:01:07,413 --> 00:01:12,167
Docker, with Docker Compose version 2. The start script checks for both.

12
00:01:12,297 --> 00:01:14,972
A Twilio account, or a Plivo account.

13
00:01:15,102 --> 00:01:19,344
A phone number on that account. It goes into your .env file.

14
00:01:19,474 --> 00:01:21,240
An ngrok authtoken.

15
00:01:21,370 --> 00:01:28,303
And API keys for the providers your agent
will use: a transcriber, an LLM, and a voice.

16
00:01:28,953 --> 00:01:38,526
Start from the sample. Populate a .env file from .env.sample. The
compose file loads .env into the Bolna app and the telephony servers.

17
00:01:38,656 --> 00:01:48,579
Add your provider keys: Deepgram for transcription, ElevenLabs for the
voice, and OpenAI for the LLM, matching the agent you'll create.

18
00:01:48,709 --> 00:01:57,230
The Redis URL already points at the redis
container, on port 6379. Leave it as it is.

19
00:01:57,360 --> 00:02:02,892
For Twilio, fill in the account SID, the auth token, and your Twilio phone number.

20
00:02:03,022 --> 00:02:13,116
For Plivo, the auth ID, the auth token, and your Plivo phone
number. The sample also has slots for Soniox, and a self-hosted transcriber.

21
00:02:13,766 --> 00:02:16,352
The second file is the ngrok config.

22
00:02:16,482 --> 00:02:24,522
Replace the auth token placeholder with your own ngrok
authtoken. The README calls this out as a required step.

23
00:02:24,652 --> 00:02:39,286
It defines an HTTP tunnel for each app: Twilio on 8001, Plivo on 8002,
and Bolna on 5001. The ngrok container mounts this file, and starts all the tunnels.

24
00:02:39,936 --> 00:02:42,597
The easiest path is the provided script.

25
00:02:42,727 --> 00:02:45,176
Change into the local setup folder,

26
00:02:45,306 --> 00:02:47,823
make start dot sh executable,

27
00:02:47,953 --> 00:02:59,507
and run it. It checks that Docker and the Docker Compose v2 CLI
are installed, enables BuildKit, builds every service, and starts them in detached mode.

28
00:02:59,637 --> 00:03:07,379
Then docker compose ps shows the running containers,
and docker compose logs, dash f, follows the logs.

29
00:03:08,029 --> 00:03:12,260
Prefer to run it by hand? It is the same steps the script runs.

30
00:03:12,390 --> 00:03:14,855
Enable BuildKit for faster builds,

31
00:03:14,985 --> 00:03:16,595
with these two exports.

32
00:03:16,725 --> 00:03:19,701
Build the images with docker compose build.

33
00:03:19,831 --> 00:03:35,814
Then start the services. You don't need both telephony servers. Run the Bolna app with only the Twilio app,
or only the Plivo app. Compose also starts what they depend on. Plain docker compose up, dash d, starts everything.

34
00:03:36,464 --> 00:03:39,807
Three details in the compose file are worth knowing.

35
00:03:39,937 --> 00:03:45,977
An agent data folder, one level above local setup, is mounted into the Bolna app.

36
00:03:46,107 --> 00:03:58,986
Your AWS credentials and config are mounted, read only. That is how
AWS Polly reaches system wide credentials, through your home folder's dot AWS directory.

37
00:03:59,116 --> 00:04:06,762
And Redis is the persistent storage for agents and
prompt data. The sample's Redis URL points straight at it.

38
00:04:07,412 --> 00:04:14,023
With the containers up, the README says you
can create agents, and instruct them to initiate calls.

39
00:04:14,153 --> 00:04:25,089
You create an agent on the Bolna server, on port 5001, by
posting the agent JSON to slash agent. The next episode covers that schema.

40
00:04:25,219 --> 00:04:28,883
It returns an agent ID, with the state created.

41
00:04:29,013 --> 00:04:41,778
Then you ask your telephony server to call with that agent. The README doesn't
spell out that request, so read it in twilio_api_server.py, or plivo_api_server.py, in local setup.

42
00:04:41,908 --> 00:04:48,743
The provider places the call, and the
conversation streams between telephony and Bolna over websockets.

43
00:04:49,393 --> 00:04:53,493
If the local setup never places a call, check these, in order.

44
00:04:53,623 --> 00:04:59,980
The start script stops early if Docker, or the Docker Compose v2 CLI, is missing.

45
00:05:00,110 --> 00:05:05,009
The .env file is filled from the sample, with the keys your agent uses.

46
00:05:05,139 --> 00:05:09,622
The ngrok config has your real authtoken, not the placeholder.

47
00:05:09,752 --> 00:05:18,563
The telephony app you chose is running. Starting the Bolna app with the
Plivo app means there is no Twilio server, and the other way round.

48
00:05:18,693 --> 00:05:22,734
Your Twilio or Plivo phone number and credentials are set.

49
00:05:22,864 --> 00:05:27,510
And docker compose logs, dash f, shows which container is failing.

50
00:05:28,160 --> 00:05:29,258
Quick recap.

51
00:05:29,388 --> 00:05:34,582
Four containers: a telephony server, the Bolna server, ngrok, and Redis.

52
00:05:34,712 --> 00:05:37,500
Populate your .env file from the sample.

53
00:05:37,630 --> 00:05:39,601
Add your ngrok authtoken.

54
00:05:39,731 --> 00:05:43,729
Run start dot sh, or docker compose up, dash d.

55
00:05:43,859 --> 00:05:46,617
And run only the telephony server you need.

56
00:05:46,747 --> 00:05:53,999
Next: Bolna open source in Python, with the
examples, the agent JSON, and the agent API.

57
00:05:54,129 --> 00:05:59,808
This masterclass is created by Omkar Ghate. See you in episode fifty six.
